  "term": "cannabinoid receptor",
  "definition": "A cannabinoid receptor is a type of G-protein-coupled receptor that responds to cannabinoids, including compounds from cannabis and the body’s own endocannabinoids. These receptors may help regulate the release of signaling substances such as neurotransmitters and cytokines.",
